    <p class="eyebrow rv">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="rv page-title">What this site<br>collects about you.</h1>
    <p class="lede rv">Almost nothing. This is a set of static files. It runs no analytics, sets no cookies and, unless you press play on a video, loads nothing from another company's servers.</p>

    <h2 class="rv as-h3">No cookies, no analytics, no tracking</h2>
    <p class="rv">The public pages set no cookies. They store nothing in your browser beyond the ordinary cache. There is no analytics package, no tag manager, no advertising pixel and no social media widget. Nothing on any page reports your visit to a third party.</p>
    <p class="rv">Every font, image, stylesheet, script, map file and audio file is served from this site. Nothing is loaded from a content delivery network, a font service or an image host, so no other company sees your request simply because you opened a page here.</p>

    <h2 class="rv as-h3">Links out</h2>
    <p class="rv">Several pages link to other sites: Coillte, d&#250;chas.ie, the National Biodiversity Data Centre, Wikimedia Commons, Invasive Species Ireland, catchments.ie and others. Those are ordinary links. Nothing loads from them until you choose to follow one, and once you do you are on their site under their privacy policy, not this one.</p>
    <p class="rv">The home page can show a few of the group&#8217;s Instagram and Facebook posts. Each is a card with a caption written by the group and an ordinary link to the post. Nothing is loaded from Instagram, Facebook or Meta to show them, and there is no Meta script or pixel on any page.</p>

    <h2 class="rv as-h3">Videos</h2>
    <p class="rv">Some news posts include a video. Until you press play, the post shows a still image and a play button, both served from this site: nothing is loaded from YouTube or Google, and nothing about your visit is recorded by them.</p>
    <p class="rv">Pressing play loads YouTube&#8217;s player from youtube-nocookie.com, its privacy-enhanced mode, and the player then fetches the video and its controls from other Google servers. YouTube is owned by Google. From that moment Google receives your IP address and the usual technical information about your browser, may store information in your browser, and its own privacy policy applies. If you never press play, none of that happens.</p>

    <h2 class="rv as-h3">The map, and your position</h2>
    <p class="rv">The map on the trails page has a button that shows where you are. If you press it, your browser will ask your permission and then work out your position on your device. That position is drawn on the map in your browser and is not sent to this site, stored, or shared with anyone. If you never press the button, your position is never requested. If you refuse the permission, the rest of the map works exactly as before.</p>

    <h2 class="rv as-h3">Hosting</h2>
    <p class="rv">The site is hosted by Netlify. Like any web host, Netlify's servers process the technical information your browser sends in order to deliver the page: your IP address, the page requested, the time, and your browser and operating system. C&#225;irde Corrin does not read those logs and does not receive a copy of them. What Netlify does with them is governed by Netlify's own privacy notice and its terms as a processor.</p>

    <h2 class="rv as-h3">The news editor</h2>
    <p class="rv">The site has one area that is not public: the news editor at /admin/, where the people who write news posts log in. It is not linked from any page, search engines are asked to leave it alone, and you never load it by visiting the site.</p>
    <p class="rv">The public pages still make no third-party requests. The news editor, which requires a login, exchanges requests with Netlify to authenticate the editor and to save their posts and photos. Its own scripts are served from this site, not from a content delivery network. Logging in sets one cookie, holding the login, in that editor&#8217;s browser, and the editor keeps the login, and a copy of any unsaved draft, in that browser&#8217;s storage.</p>
    <p class="rv">For each editor, Netlify holds the email address, a name if one is given, and the password in a form that cannot be read back. Each post or photo an editor saves is recorded in the site&#8217;s change history with that editor&#8217;s name and email address.</p>

    <h2 class="rv as-h3">Email</h2>
    <p class="rv">If you write to <a href="mailto:hello@cairdecorrin.ie">hello@cairdecorrin.ie</a>, we hold your message and your email address for as long as we need them to deal with what you wrote about, and to keep a record of what was agreed. We do not add you to a mailing list, and we do not pass your address to anyone else. There is no sign-up form anywhere on this site.</p>

    <h2 class="rv as-h3">Photographs of people</h2>
    <p class="rv">No photograph on this site shows an identifiable person. Written consent is held for the photographs in the group&#8217;s archive that do, so any published here later will carry it.</p>

    <h2 class="rv as-h3">Your rights</h2>
    <p class="rv">Under the General Data Protection Regulation you may ask what personal data we hold about you, ask for it to be corrected or deleted, and complain to the Data Protection Commission. Unless you are one of the news editors, the only personal data we hold is email correspondence you started, so a request will usually be answered by telling you what is in the inbox and deleting it if you ask. Write to <a href="mailto:hello@cairdecorrin.ie">hello@cairdecorrin.ie</a>.</p>

    <h2 class="rv as-h3">Changes</h2>
    <p class="rv">If the site starts doing something this page does not describe, this page changes first. Anything added later that collects information, such as a sign-up form or an event booking, will be described here before it goes live.</p>
